# Every env file at any depth, then re-include only the committed examples.
#
# Two mistakes were made here in turn. First, listing `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.*.local` individually missed `.env.docker` — the file the README tells
# you to create and fill with secrets. Then `.env*` alone still missed
# `apps/api/.env`, because a pattern without `**/` only matches the context
# root; that file really did end up at /app/.env in a built image, carrying
# DATABASE_URL and both JWT secrets.
#
# A layer keeps whatever it copied, so deleting the file later does not undo it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example

docs
README.md
PROJECT_PLAN.md
